/*Q2. You are designing a class hierarchy to model a music playlist. Implement the required functionality using abstract classes, inheritance,
constructors, and method overriding.
Create an abstract class named Song with:
• A String variable title representing the title of the song.
• A parameterized constructor to initialize title.
• An abstract method play() that displays a message indicating that the song is playing.
Mp3Song
Create a class named Mp3Song that extends Song.
The class must contain:
• A double variable fileSize representing the size of the MP3 file.
• A parameterized constructor that initializes the inherited title and fileSize.
• An overridden play() method that displays:
Playing MP3 song: <title>
StreamingSong
Create a class named StreamingSong that extends Song.
The class must contain:
• A boolean variable isHighQuality indicating whether the song is streamed in high quality.
• A parameterized constructor that initializes the inherited title and isHighQuality.
• An overridden play() method that displays:
Streaming <quality> quality song: <title>
where <quality> is:
• high when isHighQuality is true
• normal when isHighQuality is false
In the main() method:
1. Create a Scanner object.
2. Read the MP3 song title.
3. Read the MP3 file size as a double.
4. Create an Mp3Song object using the entered values.
5. Invoke its play() method.
6. Read the streaming song title.
7. Read the high-quality status as a boolean.
8. Create a StreamingSong object using the entered values.
9. Invoke its play() method.
10. Close the Scanner.
Input Format:
The input consists of the following values in order:
• One line containing the title of the MP3 song.
• One line containing the MP3 file size as a double.
• One line containing the title of the streaming song.
• One line containing a boolean value indicating whether the streaming song is in high quality. The value can be case-insensitive.
Each value is provided on a separate line.
Output Format:
Display the playback messages in the same order as the songs are created:
Playing MP3 song: <mp3_title>
Streaming <quality> quality song: <streaming title>
*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
abstract class Song {
    String title;
 
    Song(String title) {
        this.title = title;
    }
 
    abstract void play();
}
 
class Mp3Song extends Song {
    double fileSize;
 
    Mp3Song(String title, double fileSize) {
        super(title);
        this.fileSize = fileSize;
    }
 
    @Override
    void play() {
        System.out.println("Playing MP3 song: " + title);
    }
}
 
class StreamingSong extends Song {
    boolean isHighQuality;
 
    StreamingSong(String title, boolean isHighQuality) {
        super(title);
        this.isHighQuality = isHighQuality;
    }
 
    @Override
    void play() {
        String quality = isHighQuality ? "high" : "normal";
        System.out.println("Streaming " + quality + " quality song: " + title);
    }
}
 
public class MusicPlaylist {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        String mp3Title = sc.nextLine().trim();
        double size = Double.parseDouble(sc.nextLine().trim());
        Song mp3 = new Mp3Song(mp3Title, size);
        mp3.play();
        String streamTitle = sc.nextLine().trim();
        boolean hq = Boolean.parseBoolean(sc.nextLine().trim());   // case-insensitive
        Song stream = new StreamingSong(streamTitle, hq);
        stream.play();
        sc.close();
    }
}
